 "description": "Short authentication string (SAS) vectors for pairing (docs/specs/2026-11-01-pairing-and-trust.md). digest = SHA-256(ASCII 'gander-sas-v1' || host_spki || device_nonce || host_nonce), plain concatenation, no length prefixes. host_spki is the DER-encoded SubjectPublicKeyInfo of the host's leaf certificate as seen in the TLS handshake (the same bytes whose SHA-256, base64url without padding, is host_id), NOT its hash. device_nonce and host_nonce are the raw 16 bytes (base64url-decoded from the wire), device first. first_20_bits = digest[0]<<12 | digest[1]<<4 | digest[2]>>4 (big-endian). Because 20 bits reach 1048575 (7 digits) the code is first_20_bits mod 1000000, zero-padded to 6 digits ('sas_digits') and displayed as 3+3 digits separated by one space ('sas'). The keys are public P-256 points (G and 2G), not real host keys; nonces are fixed test inputs. Rust runner: host/gander-core/tests/sas_vectors.rs.",
